Diagnostic placeholders are intended for troubleshooting rather than stable player-facing HUD content. An allowlisted source can still be unknown until Starfield publishes usable data.

[size=3][b][u]Text formats and templates[/u][/b][/size]
Supported formats are [font=Courier New]raw[/font], [font=Courier New]integer[/font], [font=Courier New]percent[/font], [font=Courier New]temperature[/font], [font=Courier New]gravity[/font], [font=Courier New]time24[/font], and [font=Courier New]boolean[/font]. Use placeholders such as [font=Courier New]{player.health:integer}[/font]. Templates allow 1 through 8 variables and up to 256 characters. Unknown values show the complete fallback.

[size=3][b][u]Building blocks and composites[/u][/b][/size]
[list]
[*][font=Courier New]group[/font], [font=Courier New]text[/font], [font=Courier New]panel[/font], [font=Courier New]shape[/font], [font=Courier New]divider[/font], and [font=Courier New]mask[/font] build the layout.[/*]
[*][font=Courier New]meter[/font] displays bounded health, oxygen, CO2, boost, or progress values.[/*]
[*][font=Courier New]svg[/font], [font=Courier New]path[/font], [font=Courier New]icon[/font], [font=Courier New]symbol[/font], and [font=Courier New]providerSymbol[/font] display approved artwork.[/*]
[*][font=Courier New]button[/font], [font=Courier New]quickBar[/font], [font=Courier New]informationPanel[/font], and [font=Courier New]warning[/font] provide supported composites.[/*]
[*][font=Courier New]instance[/font], [font=Courier New]repeater[/font], [font=Courier New]state[/font], and [font=Courier New]override[/font] reuse bounded content.[/*]
[/list]

[size=3][b][u]Bethesda display filters[/u][/b][/size]
The optional [font=Courier New]<vanillaVisibility>[/font] block can affect only [font=Courier New]topCenter[/font], [font=Courier New]bottomLeft[/font], [font=Courier New]rightMeters[/font], [font=Courier New]socialCommandIcons[/font], [font=Courier New]floatingQuestMarkers[/font], and [font=Courier New]crewBuffWidget[/font].

Use [font=Courier New]offsetX[/font] and [font=Courier New]offsetY[/font] together for relative placement, or [font=Courier New]x[/font], [font=Courier New]y[/font], and [font=Courier New]anchor[/font] together for absolute placement. These filters respect Starfield's own visibility and opacity and cannot replace enemy health, stealth, reticles, crosshairs, or other vanilla-owned behavior.

[size=3][b][u]Limits and unsupported features[/u][/b][/size]
[list]
[*]16 root includes; 64 templates; 512 resolved components; 64 repeater items.[/*]
[*]16 state choices; 16 quick-bar buttons; 20 information items; 12 information rows.[/*]
[*]64 meter parts; 5 scanner targets; 8 text-template variables.[/*]
[*]SVGs allow 256 elements and 16 nesting levels.[/*]
[*]Arbitrary scripts, providers, nested imports, live palette switching, raster images, network paths, external SWF libraries, and unsupported Bethesda ownership changes are not available.[/*]
[/list]

The HUD loads as one complete layer. Fix the first diagnostic, keep [font=Courier New]schemaVersion="1"[/font] and [font=Courier New]runtimeVersion="1"[/font], fully restart Starfield, and test each game state.
